# 9. Core Features

## 9.1 Student Profiles

Students can create profiles containing:

* Name
* Skills
* Interests
* Experience
* Availability
* Portfolio
* GitHub profile
* Research interests
* Completed projects

The profile is designed to help other students understand what a potential collaborator can contribute.

---

# 10. Team Discovery

Students can discover potential collaborators using filters such as:

* Skills
* Interests
* Academic branch
* Availability
* Research domain

The goal is to make team formation more meaningful than simply choosing people based on familiarity.

---

# 11. Project Collaboration

Students can:

* Create projects
* Join existing projects
* Invite teammates
* Assign tasks
* Track progress
* Share updates
* Monitor deadlines

Each project can have its own collaborative workspace.

---

# 12. Project Showcase

Each project can have a dedicated showcase page.

The showcase can contain:

* Project description
* Project status
* Screenshots
* UI designs
* Technology stack
* GitHub repository
* Live demo
* Team members
* Project achievements

### Projects in the Planning Stage

Projects do not necessarily need to be completed before being showcased.

Students can present planned projects using:

* Project descriptions
* Generated concept images
* Figma designs
* UI prototypes
* Planned technology stacks
* Expected features

This allows students to attract collaborators even before development begins.

